 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd and ironic; the joke is on the hiding places, never on a victim (none appears). The Chilean passenger (Barcelona, March 2009) was ARRESTED only and no court outcome was found: never named, drawn ONLY as a dark rim-lit silhouette tagged NOT A LIKENESS, seated with crutches, every claim attributed ('police say', ARRESTED, AS OF OCT 2026); the self-inflicted-injury theory is stated on screen as a possibility investigators examined, not a finding. The seven people arrested in the Madrid pineapple case (2018) are accused only, never named and not drawn. Nobody is drawn as a suspect in the frozen-sharks case (no arrest reported). The customs officer, the plain-clothes inspector and the navy inspector are generic figures with no insignia; no weapon shown or mentioned; no force shown. The sharks are frozen carcasses in a cargo container (dead fish as freight, as reported), no animal is harmed on screen. The customs room, the X-ray monitor (a generic bone image), the wholesale market and the port are illustrations, not reported scenes; the sign reads only CUSTOMS in plain type (no force name, flag or crest); the cast, the pineapples and the sharks are drawn generically. Every card is our own typed graphic; no dialogue or quotation card. Facts verified 2026-10-20.",
