 "claims": [
  {
   "id": "K_hook",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "March 2009: Spanish police arrested a 66-year-old Chilean man at Barcelona's El Prat airport, arriving from Santiago, Chile, wearing a leg cast made of compressed cocaine (police: the first cast they had seen made entirely of the drug; it weighed about a kilogram). Narration: 'Police say his leg cast was made of cocaine.' Headline 'A LEG CAST / MADE OF COCAINE'. Accused only: never named, silhouette.",
   "sources": [
    "nbcap",
    "police1cast",
    "rnz",
    "rte",
    "emol"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_total",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Altogether he carried about 5 kg of cocaine (AP: 'about 5 kilograms (11 pounds)'; RNZ: 4.85 kg). Narration: '5 kilos.'",
   "sources": [
    "nbcap",
    "police1cast",
    "rnz",
    "rte"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_cans",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "More cocaine was hidden in six beer cans that had been emptied, packed with the drug and resealed, and inside the legs of two small folding stools. Narration: 'Cocaine inside six beer cans.' (No report mentions seat covers.)",
   "sources": [
    "nbcap",
    "police1cast",
    "rte",
    "emol"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_spray",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Police detected the drug by spraying the cast with a chemical reagent that turns bright blue on contact with cocaine. Narration (gotcha): 'One spray test. The cast turned bright blue.' Callout 'TURNED BRIGHT BLUE'.",
   "sources": [
    "nbcap",
    "police1cast",
    "rnz",
    "abc6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_arrest",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "He was arrested at the airport (reported 6 March 2009); no plea, trial or sentence was found in any extract, so the reel says accused/arrested only. Label 'ARRESTED · EL PRAT, BARCELONA · MARCH 2009 · POLICE SAY', 'no court outcome found · as of Oct 2026'.",
   "sources": [
    "nbcap",
    "rte",
    "emol",
    "rnz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_pine",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "August 2018: Spanish National Police seized about 67 kg of cocaine hidden inside dozens of hollowed-out pineapples at Mercamadrid, Madrid's main wholesale fruit and vegetable market; each pineapple was hollowed and filled with compact cylinders of the drug. Narration: 'Pineapples. Hollowed out, packed with cocaine.' Label 'MERCAMADRID, MADRID · AUG 2018'.",
   "sources": [
    "dailymav",
    "inquirer",
    "thelocal",
    "euronews",
    "ticotimes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_wax",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "FUN FACT: each pineapple held roughly 800 g to 1 kg of cocaine, and the fruit was sealed with wax to mask the chemical smell. Card 'EACH PINEAPPLE: ABOUT A KILO / SEALED WITH WAX / TO HIDE THE SMELL'.",
   "sources": [
    "inquirer",
    "thelocal",
    "dailymav",
    "eju"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_seized",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "STATISTIC (counter 67 KG): the seizure at the Madrid market was 67 kg (148 lb); seven people were arrested, three in Madrid and four in Barcelona. Narration (gotcha): 'Caught at Madrid's market. 67 kilos. Seven arrested.' Label 'SEVEN ARRESTED · 3 MADRID, 4 BARCELONA'. Accused only; nobody named.",
   "sources": [
    "dailymav",
    "inquirer",
    "thelocal",
    "ticotimes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_route",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The pineapples came from Costa Rica by ship to the Portuguese port of Setubal and then overland to Madrid.",
   "sources": [
    "dailymav",
    "inquirer",
    "thelocal",
    "ticotimes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_sharks",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "June 2009, Progreso, Yucatan, Mexico: the Mexican navy found cocaine packed inside more than 20 frozen shark carcasses in two containers shipped from Costa Rica aboard the freighter Dover Strait. Narration: 'Then Mexico. Frozen sharks.' Label 'PROGRESO, YUCATAN · JUNE 2009'. No arrest reported in the extracts; nobody drawn as a suspect.",
   "sources": [
    "nbcsd",
    "police1sharks",
    "nbcreuters",
    "aljazeera",
    "nbcny"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_xray",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The find began with routine X-ray inspections of the two containers (Reuters/Al Jazeera: X-ray machines and sniffer dogs); officers cut the sharks open to find the slabs of cocaine inside. Narration (gotcha): 'Navy X-rays caught it.' Callout 'FLAGGED BY X-RAY'.",
   "sources": [
    "nbcsd",
    "police1sharks",
    "nbcreuters",
    "aljazeera"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_ton",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The haul: 893 kg (1,965 lb) in 870 packages according to prosecutors (AP); Reuters reported 'more than a ton'. Narration: 'Nearly a ton.' (AP's own headline: 'Almost one ton'.) Label '893 KG IN 870 PACKAGES · PROSECUTORS (AP) · REUTERS: OVER A TON'.",
   "sources": [
    "nbcsd",
    "police1sharks",
    "nbcreuters",
    "aljazeera",
    "latercera"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_leg",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "X-rays showed the man's leg really was broken (an open fracture of the left tibia and fibula); investigators examined whether the injury had been inflicted deliberately to get the cast through security, a possibility, not a finding. Narration (callback): 'And his leg? Really broken.' Label 'X-RAYS SHOWED A REAL FRACTURE · POLICE'.",
   "sources": [
    "nbcap",
    "police1cast",
    "rnz",
    "emol",
    "rte"
   ]
  }
 ],
